@page "/help"
@attribute [Authorize]
<PageTitle>Help · InstrumentHub</PageTitle>
<div class="page-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">A LITTLE GUIDANCE</div><h1>Help & support</h1><p>Make the most of your instrument workspace.</p></div></div>
<div class="help-content"><section class="panel settings-card"><h2>Managing instruments</h2><p>Choose Add instrument to register equipment. Select an instrument’s name in the table to edit its details, owner, dates, manual status, or calibration task result.</p><h2>Planning calibrations</h2><p>Use the Overdue or Due Soon stat cards to filter the schedule. The Filters button provides all calibration health and task-result filters. Click Due date to sort by the earliest scheduled date.</p><h2>Certificates and audit records</h2><p>Upload a PDF directly from the instrument table, or choose an instrument in the Certificates screen. Files must be genuine PDF documents of 10 MB or less. Uploads preserve the calibration dates and task result; update those in the instrument details after reviewing the certificate.</p><h2>Imports and exports</h2><p>Inventory accepts CSV and XLSX files up to 5 MB and 500 rows. Required columns are AssetId, Name, and Department. Optional columns are Model, Location, Owner, CurrentStatus, and NextDueDate. Use yyyy-MM-dd for dates. CurrentStatus accepts Active, In Repair, or Out of Service. Imports add new records and reject duplicate asset IDs. Export downloads a CSV of the entire inventory.</p><h2>Repairs</h2><p>Log an issue and assign a technician from Repair Logs. The instrument becomes In Repair. Completing all open work orders returns it to Active, and its calibration health is recalculated from its due date.</p><h2>Understanding compliance</h2><p>Compliance counts Calibrated and Due Soon instruments, divided by all instruments except Out of Service. Availability uses the same available count divided by the total inventory. In Repair, Overdue, and Pending Calibration assets are not counted as available.</p></section></div>
